    "description": "The Kannimara Teak is one of the world's biggest living teak (Tectona grandis) trees. It is found at Parambikulam Tiger Reserve in Palakkad district, Kerala. It stands at a height of 41.83 meters and has a girth of 7.24 meters (measured at breast height), with an estimated age of approximately 500 years. In recognition of its significance, the Government of India awarded the tree the Mahavriksha Puraskar (Great Tree Award) in 1994.",
